Nearly true.

In the case of NAO, which dumps you immediately into dgamelauncher, I
have found that if you adjust your window after connecting to make it
FEWER than 25 lines, then start playing nethack, it notices and
respects the change. But making it MORE than 25 lines is not respected
after connecting.

But if you use Putty to connect to some other unix site where you have
a shell account, change around the window size after connecting (by
dragging the window), and THEN start nethack, the window size change is
respected.

So, it appears to be dgamelauncher that won't let you increase the line
count after connecting.

> on the putty screen before you connect, on
